###############################################################################
# Onboarding walkthrough — take a fresh install to a working bot.
# Run the requests top to bottom.
#
# Prerequisites (the flow will not complete without these):
#   1. docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml up -d     # pgvector + mongo
#   2. ollama pull nomic-embed-text                          # EMBED_MODEL
#      ollama pull mistral:latest                            # your BASE_MODEL
#   3. npm run dev:start
#
# The models named by BASE_MODEL / TOOL_MODEL / EMBED_MODEL are auto-registered
# in the llmModel collection at startup, but Ollama must actually have them
# pulled — otherwise ingestion fails with a 404 from the embeddings endpoint.
###############################################################################

@host = http://localhost:3000

### 0. Health — both dependencies must report "up" before continuing.
GET {{host}}/health

### 1. Register. Returns an access token; the refresh token arrives as a cookie.
POST {{host}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@gmail.com",
  "password": "Testing@123"
}

### 2. Login (use this if the account already exists).
# @name login
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@gmail.com",
  "password": "Testing@123"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### 3. Which models are registered? Bot creation fails unless BASE_MODEL and
###    EMBED_MODEL both appear here.
GET {{host}}/llm
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Available bot types.
GET {{host}}/metadata/bot-type
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Create a bot.
###    KB_Bot          — answers only from uploaded documents (own vector table)
###    General_Purpose — answers from the model's own knowledge, no retrieval
# @name createBot
POST {{host}}/bots
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "botName": "Support Bot",
  "botDesc": "Answers questions from the support handbook",
  "botType": "KB_Bot",
  "owner": "john.doe@gmail.com"
}

###
@botId = {{createBot.response.body.data.botId}}

### 6. List your bots (handy if you lost the botId above).
GET {{host}}/bots/owner/john.doe@gmail.com
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Upload a document. Supported: pdf, docx, doc, pptx, txt (max 25 MB).
###    Re-uploading identical content is a no-op — dedup is by file hash.
###    Point the `< ./path` line at a real file next to this .http file.
POST {{host}}/kb/upload/{{botId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="handbook.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./sample-handbook.txt
------Boundary--

### 8. Confirm what the bot has ingested.
GET {{host}}/kb/bot-id/{{botId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Chat — should answer from the uploaded document.
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "botId": "{{botId}}",
  "question": "What is the refund policy?"
}

### 10. Off-topic question — a KB_Bot should decline rather than invent an answer.
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "botId": "{{botId}}",
  "question": "What is the capital of Mongolia?"
}

### 11. Optional: register a tool the bot can call. See tool.http for the full
###     shape, including auth modes and parameter definitions.
POST {{host}}/tools
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "botId": "{{botId}}",
  "name": "get_weather",
  "description": "Fetches the current weather for a given city.",
  "type": "API",
  "endpoint": "http://api.weatherapi.com/v1/current.json",
  "method": "GET",
  "auth": {
    "type": "apiKey",
    "apiKey": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_KEY",
    "apiKeyLocation": "query",
    "apiKeyName": "key"
  },
  "queryParam": [
    {
      "name": "q",
      "description": "The city to get weather for.",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true
    }
  ],
  "enabled": true,
  "systemPrompt": "Summarise the weather in one friendly sentence. Do not show raw JSON."
}

### 12. Tool-routed question. The tool model decides whether to call the tool;
###     if it declines or the call fails, the request falls back to normal RAG.
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "botId": "{{botId}}",
  "question": "What is the weather in Mumbai?"
}
